  "summary": "The identified studies directly applying contrastive learning—specifically 'Representation Learning With Paired Positive And Negative Examples'—to energy demand forecasting report varied performance across different datasets. Duarte et al. [V0142] achieved a Mean Absolute Error (MAE) of 0.67 on the ProtMap dataset, while Chen et al. [V0141] reported an accuracy of 0.6 on GridWatch. Fischer et al. [V0144] utilized the ChurnBench dataset to obtain an F1 score of 0.81, and El-Sayed et al. [V0143] reported an AUROC of 0.74 on FireScope. Document [V0149] is included in the ranking as it explicitly discusses prior work applying this specific representation learning method to electricity consumption, though it applies a different method (Self-Attention Encoder) itself. Other documents mentioning prior work were excluded from the primary ranking as they do not constitute direct applications.",
